(477134, 44672, 5475, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for the great comments!  Although I had Jonah sit where I could use by Alien Bee 800 with a brolley box, it is still somewhat a candid because he never cooperates and I don''t pose him.  He sat there for a minute or so and did what he did, and I was lucky enough to get a wonderful shot with just one photo!<br/>This is pretty much straight out of the camera, converted to grayscale using the channel mixer in Photoshop.  The only other editing was a light pass with the dodge tool for the eye highlights.  I never thought I''d see the day that a child photo would win a challenge here, let alone one of mine!  Thank you all for your votes and comments!<br/>JD Anderson<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-08 02:14:27.</i></td>', 'Thank you everyone for the great comments!  Although I had Jonah sit where I could use by Alien Bee 800 with a brolley box, it is still somewhat a candid because he never cooperates and I don''t pose him.  He sat there for a minute or so and did what he did, and I was lucky enough to get a wonderful shot with just one photo!This is pretty much straight out of the camera, converted to grayscale using the channel mixer in Photoshop.  The only other editing was a light pass with the dodge tool for the eye highlights.  I never thought I''d see the day that a child photo would win a challenge here, let alone one of mine!  Thank you all for your votes and comments!JD Anderson', '2003-11-08 02:13:39.000000', '2003-11-08 02:14:27.000000', 0),
